1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,877
Wingard Cottage: a perfect family getaway on a pristine lake, with a long history of

2
00:00:04,877 --> 00:00:05,313
tragedy.

3
00:00:05,533 --> 00:00:07,283
Here's how the location plays.

4
00:00:08,100 --> 00:00:11,196
Lay the four Supply Item cards face up in the play area.

5
00:00:11,196 --> 00:00:15,010
Shuffle the ten Crafted Item cards and deal four face up beside them.

6
00:00:15,010 --> 00:00:16,889
Those four are what you can build.

7
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:21,312
The House means the Kitchen, both Bedrooms, the Bathroom, the Family Room, the

8
00:00:21,312 --> 00:00:23,119
Foyer, the Laundry Room and the Garage.

9
00:00:23,339 --> 00:00:26,255
Indoors means the House plus the Shed and the Boathouse.

10
00:00:26,255 --> 00:00:29,952
Everything else is an outdoor space. Lots of cards care which is which.

11
00:00:30,767 --> 00:00:34,927
Some spaces show a Supply symbol: Discarded Tools, Nails, Rope or Wood.

12
00:00:35,147 --> 00:00:39,454
While on one of those spaces, not just passing through, you can spend one Time to

13
00:00:39,454 --> 00:00:42,379
take that Supply Item card. It goes in a Backpack slot.

14
00:00:42,599 --> 00:00:47,091
When a Supply card is discarded, it goes back face up in the play area, ready to be

15
00:00:47,091 --> 00:00:47,740
taken again.

16
00:00:48,567 --> 00:00:53,246
To craft, discard the Item and Supply cards listed on a face-up Crafted Item, pay

17
00:00:53,246 --> 00:00:56,481
its Time cost, and take it into a Hand or Backpack slot.

18
00:00:56,701 --> 00:00:59,162
For example: Ava has a Wooden Bat and Nails.

19
00:00:59,162 --> 00:01:03,635
She pays two Time to craft the Nail Bat, discards the Bat, and returns the Nails

20
00:01:03,635 --> 00:01:04,083
face up.

21
00:01:04,303 --> 00:01:09,043
Used items keep their remaining uses: a Shotgun with one shot left makes a Sawed-off

22
00:01:09,043 --> 00:01:13,671
Shotgun with one shot left. Discarded Crafted Items go back face up, to be crafted

23
00:01:13,671 --> 00:01:14,009
again.

24
00:01:14,833 --> 00:01:19,193
Some standouts. Nail Traps and Snares cost one Time to place in your space, and

25
00:01:19,193 --> 00:01:21,511
damage or stop the next Enemy that enters.

26
00:01:21,731 --> 00:01:25,856
The Sawed-off Shotgun spends a Time to deal three damage to its target and two to

27
00:01:25,856 --> 00:01:29,624
every other Enemy there. The Spear can shove an Enemy into the next space.

28
00:01:29,844 --> 00:01:34,081
The Obliterator hits for three but slows you, and costs you health for every one you

29
00:01:34,081 --> 00:01:37,460
roll. The Brainstorming event adds two more recipes to choose from.

30
00:01:38,267 --> 00:01:42,616
Watch for Booby Traps: every Victim inside the house panics, and any Victim leaving

31
00:01:42,616 --> 00:01:43,664
the house is killed.

32
00:01:43,884 --> 00:01:48,236
Home Security can be switched on when no Enemies are in the house, keeping them out

33
00:01:48,236 --> 00:01:51,329
until three attempts or until you or a Victim go in or out.

34
00:01:51,549 --> 00:01:55,069
And one Terror card drops the Killer right into your space if you're in the house.

35
00:01:55,900 --> 00:01:59,079
A few tips. Pick up Supplies early, while the Killer is far away.

36
00:01:59,299 --> 00:02:02,008
Traps are cheap and great on the Killer's route to the Victims.

37
00:02:02,228 --> 00:02:06,270
And keep an eye on which four recipes are out before you spend items you might need.

38
00:02:06,270 --> 00:02:06,751
Good luck.

